@copilot Split the two extractor responsibilities in this PR. Update PR #20866 directly, not a new PR. In aws-lambda-events-common-2.2/library, make ApiGatewayProxyAttributesExtractor implement only AttributesExtractor<AwsLambdaRequest, Object>. Move its SpanStatusExtractor implementation into a separate package-private final ApiGatewayProxySpanStatusExtractor, and register the attributes and status extractors separately in AwsLambdaEventsInstrumenterFactory.

Preserve all existing behavior: only actual APIGatewayProxyRequestEvent inputs receive HTTP classification; status codes >=500 or <100 produce ERROR span status; otherwise preserve SpanStatusExtractor.getDefault() exception-status fallback for HTTP and non-HTTP invocations. Preserve error.type extraction, HTTP response status attributes, and response-code/exception precedence exactly. A few repeated type/status checks are acceptable; do not introduce a shared abstraction just to deduplicate the tiny predicate, and do not replace these with generic HTTP extractors that would change missing-status behavior.

Update focused tests to exercise the separate status collaborator while retaining the recently consolidated common status matrix, non-HTTP gating and default exception fallback coverage, representative library/javaagent integration status cases, propagation assertions, and both exception integration tests including event/log modes. Keep the scope to this separation and necessary test adjustments. Follow repository instructions, apply the narrowest relevant formatter directly, and run the focused tests. Acceptance criteria: attributes and span status have separate collaborators and registration, no telemetry or supported invocation behavior changes, and existing meaningful coverage is retained without reintroducing duplicate full integration matrices.

